    "body": "## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; no dependencies. It touches `sp-devonthink-store-link` only; #434 changes `sp-devonthink-insert-link` in the same file, so whichever merges second may need a trivial merge of `main`.\n\n## Problem\n\n- After selecting a sentence in a PDF opened in a separate DEVONthink viewer window, `C-c k d s` (`sp-devonthink-store-link`) said `DEVONthink has no record open in its front window`.\n- Cause: the AppleScript read only `think window 1` (the main window). A record shown in a standalone viewer window or another window is not that window.\n- The `if:` prefix in the message is Emacs's own display of an error signalled inside an `if` form, not a malformed message; I left it and reworded the message itself.\n\n## Change\n\n- The script now visits every DEVONthink window front to back (`every window`), reading `content record`, `current page` and `selected text` from each.\n- The first window with selected text wins; with no selection, the frontmost window that has a record wins.\n- Error message now says `DEVONthink has no open window with a record (open the PDF in DEVONthink first)`.\n- Doc: `sp-devonthink.org` (tangled to `sp-devonthink.el`); 2 new ERT tests; tangle check passes.\n\n## What was verified\n\n- [x] Unit tests: the script visits all windows and no longer uses `think window 1`; a multi-line selection is parsed and put in the kill ring.\n- [ ] Not verified: that DEVONthink's `every window` includes standalone viewer windows and that they expose `content record`, `current page` and `selected text` (no DEVONthink in the build environment). The AppleScript wraps each property in `try`, so a missing one is skipped rather than failing.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Open a PDF in a separate viewer window (double-click, or Open in New Window), select a sentence, switch to Emacs, `C-c k d s`: message `Stored KEY p. N (selection in the kill ring)`.\n- [ ] `M-x org-insert-link`, choose the `devonthink:` stored link: it inserts `[[devonthink:UUID::N][KEY p. N]]`; `C-y` pastes the selected sentence.\n- [ ] Repeat with the PDF in the main window and in a tab: same result.\n- [ ] Two windows open, selection only in the older one: the link points at the window with the selection.\n- [ ] No selection, one window: stores the link without a kill-ring entry.\n- [ ] Close all DEVONthink windows and run it: the new, reworded error message appears.\n- [ ] If the page is off by one, adjust `sp-devonthink-store-page-offset` and say so in the PR.\n- [ ] If it still fails, run in Script Editor: `tell application id \"DNtp\" to get class of every window` and paste the result.\n\n## Revert guide\n\n- `git revert` the single commit of this PR; nothing depends on it.\n- Reverting restores the `think window 1`-only script (it fails again for viewer windows).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC)_",
